# gh nests three deep: `gh pr create --fill`. Indented rows here are that
# nesting, and `enter` on an @ row runs that node's own --help — so anything
# not written down is still one keypress away.
name:    gh
what:    GitHub from the terminal — PRs, issues, runs, and the raw API
check:   gh
install: sudo dnf install gh   /   see cli.github.com
docs:    gh <command> --help
probe:   help
help_cmd: gh {} --help

= AM I LOGGED IN
gh auth status   | which account, which scopes, which host
gh auth login    | log in, in a browser
gh auth refresh -s SCOPE | add a scope to an existing login
gh repo view --web | open this repo in a browser

= PULL REQUESTS
@gh pr create    | open a PR from the current branch, prompting for the rest
  --fill         | use the commit messages as title and body
  --draft        | open it as a draft
  --web          | finish it in the browser
gh pr list       | open PRs in this repo
gh pr status     | the ones relevant to you, including yours
@gh pr view      | the PR for the current branch
  123 --web      | open one in a browser
gh pr diff       | the whole diff, in the terminal
gh pr checks     | the CI checks and whether they passed
gh pr checkout 123 | check out someone else's PR locally
gh pr review --approve | approve it
@gh pr merge     | merge it, prompting for how
  --squash       | one commit on the target branch
  --delete-branch | remove the branch after merging
gh pr ready      | take a draft out of draft
gh pr close 123  | close without merging

= ISSUES
gh issue list    | open issues
gh issue create  | open a new one
@gh issue view   | read one — `gh issue view 42`
  --comments     | read it with the discussion
gh issue close 42 | close it
gh issue develop 42 --checkout | branch named after the issue, checked out

= CI RUNS
gh run list      | recent workflow runs
@gh run view     | pick one and see its jobs
  --log-failed   | just the output of the steps that failed
  --job ID       | one job's log
gh run watch     | follow a run until it finishes
gh run rerun --failed | re-run only the failed jobs
gh workflow list | the workflows this repo has
gh workflow run NAME | trigger one by hand

= THE API, WHEN THERE IS NO SUBCOMMAND
@gh api          | raw JSON — `gh api repos/:owner/:repo`
  --jq '.name'   | pull one field out without needing jq installed
  --paginate     | follow every page
  -X POST -f k=v | a write request

= MISC
gh repo clone OWNER/NAME | clone, using your existing auth
gh repo fork --clone | fork and clone in one step
gh release list  | releases
gh release download TAG | fetch a release's assets
gh browse FILE   | open that file on github.com at the current commit
gh gist create F | a gist from a file

= ALL FLAGS (from --help)
